grok-4.6 and grok-4.7 are now billed by the xAI endpoint yoyo actually calls. Committed as 0eb16638 (Part of #1012). Build, tests, clippy with -D warnings and fmt check all pass.

Checked before coding: I re-read xAI's regions page today (2026-10-27). It says the US endpoint serves only grok-4.7 and grok-4.6, and that usage there "costs 10% more than on the global endpoint", with the premium covering input, output, cached input and long-context rates. That matches the reflection comment on #1012, so the plan held.

What changed for users:
• grok-4.6 on the default endpoint (https://api.x.ai/v1) was being billed 10% too high (2.20/0.55/6.60). It now bills 2.00/0.50/6.00, and 4.00/1.00/12.00 above a 200K prompt.
• grok-4.6 and grok-4.7 on `us.api.x.ai` now bill 1.1× for every rate, including the 200K+ tier. grok-4.7 there was being billed 10% too low. That was one of the three places the cost docs said read low; two remain.
• A user's own `[model_pricing]` entry is used as written and never scaled.

How:
• A new file, src/format/cost/xai_region.rs, decides whether base_url is the US endpoint, holds the 1.1× rule, and stores the answer once at startup.
• cost.rs gained 5 lines, which keeps it inside the size-gate's grace band.
• cli.rs has one call that sets the region.
• In tests, only the read of the stored setting is swapped for a per-thread value, so tests can price a request on either endpoint without racing each other.

One change from the plan: the check looks only at the URL's host, not at provider == xai as well. xAI charges the US rate for any request to us.api.x.ai, even one sent through a custom OpenAI-compatible provider.

Tests:
• New tests cover an 11-case table of URLs, which models the 1.1× applies to, prices on both endpoints (base and 200K+ tier), grok-4.5 staying unchanged on the US endpoint, and a user override staying unchanged.
• Two existing grok-4.6 assertions in price_audit_tests.rs pinned the old 10%-high rate. I updated both to the new exact values: the base rate and the 200K+ tier.
• As a check that the tests can fail, I temporarily set the premium to 1.0. Exactly the three US-side tests failed; I then restored it (no sabotage marker left).

Price audit: matched went from 70 to 71 and drifted from 31 to 30 of 114 compared. The 30 left are openai 16, google 8, zai 5, deepseek 1 and xai 0. Three of them can be picked from yoyo's model list; the other 27 are reachable only by typing --model. These numbers and the next steps are posted on #1012.

Still open: the endpoint is checked once, at startup. If the first-run setup wizard writes base_url = us.api.x.ai, that first session is billed at the base rate, 10% low. Every later session gets it right. This is noted on #1012.

