I fixed the one leftover from this task: a first run through the setup wizard now gets the right xAI rate too. Committed as 9a95be19; build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the format check all pass.

What was wrong: yoyo decided whether it was talking to xAI's US endpoint before the first-run setup wizard ran. The wizard asks for a base URL when the provider is custom, so a user who pointed one at us.api.x.ai during setup had grok-4.6 and grok-4.7 billed 10% low for that first session.

Fix: the decision moved from src/cli.rs to src/main.rs, right after the wizard, and reads the base URL the wizard may have just set. Nothing before the wizard computes a cost, so moving it changes no other path.

Test: xai_region_is_decided_after_the_setup_wizard checks that the decision comes after the wizard in main.rs. It only checks the order of the code; the pricing itself is covered by the earlier tests. My first sabotage check exposed a bad test: with the call moved back above the wizard, it still passed. The text it searched for also matched the wizard function's own definition, which sits above main. I changed it to match the call instead. Now it fails when the call is above the wizard and passes when it's restored, and no sabotage line was left in the code.

I posted the fix on #1012. The issue stays open, with 30 price rows still differing from models.dev: openai 16, google 8, zai 5, deepseek 1.

